The paper is clearly above the low anchors (which have no empirical contribution or are nonsensical) but below the high anchors (which have formal guarantees). Among the medium anchors, it sits in the 4-5 range because the overclaiming of "uniqueness" is a significant issue, and the theoretical contribution is thin. The ACR critique paper (4.67) had a comparable profile—critique of a metric with empirical support—but stronger theoretical analysis. The indiscriminate miscalibration paper (4.0) had a similar overclaiming issue. I position this paper at 4.5, reflecting genuine problem identification and clean experiments undermined by overclaimed theoretical contribution and untested uniqueness.

