HAICOSYSTEM sits between the high-scoring ToolEmu (7.33) and the medium-scoring safety benchmarks (4-6). It has a genuine contribution—the compounding risk finding and the modular framework design—but its validation is weaker than ToolEmu's and the headline 62% figure is inflated by aggressive aggregation. Compared to Agent-as-a-Judge (5.67, Reject), HAICOSYSTEM has a more substantial and original contribution. Compared to BadRobot (6.00, Poster), HAICOSYSTEM is broader in scope and identifies a more novel finding (compounding risk), but has more severe validation concerns. I place it slightly above the borderline, in the 5.5-6.0 range.

