The paper's core claim (achieving Nash equilibrium) is directly contradicted by its own evidence, the evaluation methodology is fundamentally flawed (exploitation ≠ equilibrium), and the novelty is minimal (standard Q-learning applied to a known game). It sits at or slightly above the low-scoring anchors (q2CcNvzgb7 at 3.75, GtxzVbjPKC at 3.5) — those papers at least had more theoretical content, but they share the pattern of overclaimed equilibrium convergence. The paper is below the incremental Q-learning paper at 4.0 which had theoretical contributions. I place it slightly below the closest comparable anchors.

