STSW sits above the rejected TSW-SL (6.0) due to stronger empirical results and proper spherical theoretical foundations, but below the high-scoring LSSOT/QMC-SW (7.5) whose advantages were unambiguous and well-validated. The missing tree-structure ablation — the same gap that hurt TSW-SL — prevents confident attribution of the improvements and is the primary factor holding the score down. The theoretical contribution (extending tree systems to the sphere with injectivity and metricity proofs) is genuine and solid.

