## Strengths

### Core strengths (directly support the paper's main claims)

1. **Tighter first-order characterizations of (L₀, L₁)-smooth functions enable principled method design**: Lemma 2.2 provides improved bounds (equations 3–4) that are tighter than those in Zhang et al. (2020, Corollary A.4) and Hübler et al. (2024, Lemma 8). Lemma 2.4 and Corollary 2.5 further provide novel lower bounds (equations 5–7) for the convex case, generalizing Nesterov (2018, Theorem 2.1.5). These tighter bounds are the analytic engine for the paper's improved results—they directly yield the stepsize formulas and per-step progress guarantees (equation 11) used in all subsequent convergence theorems.

